WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.275
This is the matter room, a Selerim concept for preparing legal intake.

00:00:05.275 --> 00:00:10.111
It uses thirty fictional emails and their attachments, not client records.

00:00:10.111 --> 00:00:19.342
The task is to organize the materials, identify missing information, and give a human reviewer a factual brief with inspectable sources.

00:00:19.342 --> 00:00:23.738
This guided tour uses captured application states and synthetic narration.

00:00:23.738 --> 00:00:25.936
The current pipeline is deterministic.

00:00:25.936 --> 00:00:33.409
No live language model, real law firm inbox, or external messaging service is connected in this recording.

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:37.649
The brief appears beside the source material.

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:42.346
Each factual statement has a citation naming its document, page, and line.

00:00:42.346 --> 00:00:47.042
Selecting the stated request highlights the exact line in the intake form.

00:00:47.042 --> 00:00:52.522
The reviewer can also switch to the engagement letter or open the original file.

00:00:52.522 --> 00:00:56.044
The paper surface is clearly labeled as extracted text.

00:00:56.044 --> 00:01:05.046
A requested review date is simply a fact supplied in the form; this tool does not calculate legal deadlines or offer legal advice.

00:01:06.546 --> 00:01:11.379
The needs-information view separates matters that cannot pass the configured completeness checks.

00:01:11.379 --> 00:01:17.421
In this example, the company name in the engagement letter differs from the intake form.

00:01:17.421 --> 00:01:23.463
Other fixtures contain a missing engagement letter, an unsigned letter, or a missing contact email.

00:01:23.463 --> 00:01:29.505
The application flags the specific issue and offers a route to the local follow-up queue.

00:01:29.505 --> 00:01:35.144
It does not silently repair the documents, accept the client, or send a message.

00:01:35.144 --> 00:01:38.366
All twelve planted incomplete matters were routed correctly.

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:47.641
For a complete intake, the reviewer checks the source materials and explicitly confirms that the brief has been reviewed.

00:01:47.641 --> 00:01:52.143
Approval then unlocks a separate action to file the reviewed intake.

00:01:52.143 --> 00:01:57.463
The application does not infer an attorney's decision from a document being present.

00:01:57.463 --> 00:02:02.374
This demonstration uses a local operator; it does not verify professional credentials.

00:02:02.374 --> 00:02:07.285
The server blocks approval for incomplete matters and blocks filing before approval.

00:02:07.285 --> 00:02:12.605
Changed source files also prevent the operation from completing under the old review.

00:02:14.105 --> 00:02:19.119
The filed view preserves the reviewed intake in the local demo.

00:02:19.119 --> 00:02:26.868
Filing does not establish an attorney-client relationship, clear a conflict, validate an engagement, or send any communication.

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:36.897
The runtime retains selected fields, source citations, hashes, and review metadata rather than duplicating entire PDF and email bodies in the database.

00:02:36.897 --> 00:02:40.088
Original files remain in their matter folders.

00:02:40.088 --> 00:02:46.925
Access checks reject paths outside the matter and block documents that identify a different matter.

00:02:46.925 --> 00:02:50.116
Retention still requires an explicit operator policy.

00:02:51.616 --> 00:02:56.489
The activity log makes source views and review decisions inspectable.

00:02:56.489 --> 00:03:00.388
The separate held-out evaluation contained ten fictional matters.

00:03:00.388 --> 00:03:12.083
The parser classified eighteen of eighteen documents correctly, extracted one hundred of one hundred fields, and produced fifty eight of fifty eight source-linked statements.

00:03:12.083 --> 00:03:16.956
Tests opened the cited files to verify the quoted lines.

00:03:16.956 --> 00:03:24.266
These numbers measure the generated text-PDF fixtures, not real-world legal accuracy, OCR, or model quality.

00:03:24.266 --> 00:03:27.677
The concept illustrates preparation with human oversight.

00:03:27.677 --> 00:03:34.987
A production engagement begins by defining the specific workflow, access boundaries, and measurable acceptance checks.
